          <name>kQuotaExceeded</name>
          <initializer>= 0</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>VRAM budget exceeded (cudaErrorMemoryAllocation, hipErrorOutOfMemory). Recovery: Immediate CPU fallback. Logged as non-fatal. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacethemis_1_1gpu_1a3a571daf696b6722a5ea7e8c31ce39bea93c06f92dc4e4ad3fd14ac410d9f03b5" prot="public">
          <name>kKernelTimeout</name>
          <initializer>= 1</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Kernel execution timeout (custom timeout detection via <ref refid="classthemis_1_1gpu_1_1_kernel_s_l_a_guard" kindref="compound">KernelSLAGuard</ref>). Recovery: Immediate CPU fallback with diagnostic log. Impact: SLA violation; performance impact minimal (CPU fallback active). </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacethemis_1_1gpu_1a3a571daf696b6722a5ea7e8c31ce39bea353e71b117acbf17b4d48bbd3f5ea917" prot="public">
          <name>kBackendUnavailable</name>
          <initializer>= 2</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>GPU device offline, driver error, or backend unavailable. (cudaErrorInsufficientDriver, hipErrorInsufficientDriver, etc.) Recovery: CPU fallback + mark device unavailable. Impact: Entire GPU subsystem disabled for health check duration. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacethemis_1_1gpu_1a3a571daf696b6722a5ea7e8c31ce39bea8a94b50a54fbaf74578ff9f58464e071" prot="public">
          <name>kMemoryCommunication</name>
          <initializer>= 3</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Host-to-Device or Device-to-Host transfer failure. (cudaErrorInvalidValue, cudaErrorInvalidHostPointer, etc.) Recovery: Retry once; if persists, CPU fallback. Impact: Data reliability concern; log for audit. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacethemis_1_1gpu_1a3a571daf696b6722a5ea7e8c31ce39bea11e056546dc98d05184024cc7e757eee" prot="public">
          <name>kNumerical</name>
          <initializer>= 4</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Numerical precision loss, NaN detection, or computation error. Recovery: Emit warning; continue with caution (non-blocking). Impact: Accuracy degradation; caller must validate output. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacethemis_1_1gpu_1a3a571daf696b6722a5ea7e8c31ce39beae94d8fc3b86877c5422f6546f8aea2dc" prot="public">
          <name>kUnsupportedOperation</name>
          <initializer>= 5</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Operation not supported by current device/backend/configuration. (cudaErrorNotSupported, hipErrorNotSupported, etc.) Recovery: CPU fallback; mark operation unsupported. Impact: Query degradation; correctness maintained. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacethemis_1_1gpu_1a3a571daf696b6722a5ea7e8c31ce39bea25c2dc47991b3df171ed5192bcf70390" prot="public">
          <name>kUnknown</name>
          <initializer>= 6</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
